// Title: Suspicious Extrac32 Execution
// Sigma ID: aa8e035d-7be4-48d3-a944-102aec04400d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-11-26 | Modified: 2022-08-13
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Download or Copy file with Extrac32
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Extrac32/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_extrac32.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "extrac32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\extrac32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "extrac32.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains ".cab" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/C" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Y" or ProcessCommandLine contains " \\\\")
